# README Maintenance

- When changing experiment scripts, Slurm jobs, data preparation, cache state, output paths, or backup rules, update `README.md` in the same turn.
- Keep job IDs, `RUN_NAME`, epoch counts, cache parameters, dataset readiness, and known blockers current.
- Do not document licensed dataset contents in detail; record only allowed paths, required inputs, and processing status.
- If a command submits, cancels, or replaces Slurm jobs, update the submitted-job table or note why no README change is needed.
